cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this repository, cite it as below, together with the access date. The scope note is
  part of the citation: this tool reports state transitions only.
title: >-
  sim-sentinel: Windows notifications for background simulation completion, failure, or
  stalled progress
abstract: >-
  sim-sentinel reads local simulation logs once a minute on Windows and sends a notification when
  a run finishes, fails, or stops moving. It reports state changes rather than sending a notification
  every minute. The included rules target Lumerical FDTD/EME `<project>_p0.log` files and can be
  adapted to other local text logs. Python uses only the standard library.


  SCOPE -- this is part of the citation. The tool supports Windows and local text logs only; cloud
  jobs are not covered. It does not submit or cancel simulations, and it does not judge convergence,
  energy balance, physics, or the correctness of results. The first sighting of a log establishes a
  silent baseline. Notification visibility depends on Windows settings. The process check recognizes
  names ending in `-engine.exe`; other process names require a code change for failure and stall
  detection.
